<p class="margin-top-5">As per company policy, the dormant accounts will be archived by the following stages</p>
<div>
    <h5 class="bold">1. Close Account</h5>
    <p>- If Super, Master or Agent does not have new ticket/downline in the last 3 months, he is considered as Dormant
        and his account will be closed.</p>
    <p>- Upline can reopen these closed accounts or take back their credit.</p>
</div>
<div>
    <h5 class="bold">2. Disable Account</h5>
    <p>- If Super, Master or Agent has no new ticket/downline in the last 4 months, his account will be disabled.</p>
    <p>- The remaining credit of these accounts will be cleared which lead to the same credit decreases in their
        uplines.</p>
    <p>- Upline cannot reopen disabled accounts, update customer setting or take back their given credit.</p>
</div>
<div>
    <h5 class="bold">3. Delete Settings</h5>
    <p>- If Master or Agent has no new ticket/downline in the last 7 months, his account setting will be deleted.</p>
    <p>- The remaining balance of these accounts will be automatically transferred to the upline.</p>
    <p>- Upline cannot reopen disabled accounts, view customer setting or take back their given credit.</p>
</div>
<div>
    <h5 class="bold">4. Delete Account</h5>
    <p>- A few weeks after stage 3, the account will be deleted from the system.</p>
    <p>- Upline cannot search the deleted accounts.</p>
</div>
<div class="margin-top-5">
    <p>Note: The term 'Downline' includes Direct Downline, Super Direct Member, or Master Direct Member.</p>
</div>